WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.900
[Narrator] You have built a big stage.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.200
[Narrator] And invited a global audience.

3
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.700
[Narrator] But you have just one speaker.

4
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:18.400
[Narrator] Introducing! Live translated audio! For wireless conference headsets! Every language! Right on the headsets your attendees already wear!

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:31.300
[Narrator] Think about it, organizers: every single attendee hears the room in their own language! And AV teams? It runs right through your mixer, and uses the headsets you already own!

6
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:44.600
[Narrator] The signal path? It is incredibly simple! Your mixer feeds a Mac running the app. Then the app sends those perfectly translated streams into separate channels, using your wireless headset transmitters!

7
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:55.300
[Narrator] Just watch! Channel one carries the speaker in English. And now, thanks to ConferenceCaptioning, channel two carries the live translation in French!

8
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.259
[Channel 1, a woman speaking English] Good morning, everyone, and welcome to the conference.

9
00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.593
[Channel 2, translated in a female voice] Bonjour à tous et bienvenue à la conférence.

10
00:01:03.193 --> 00:01:08.893
[Narrator] Now, a man is speaking, so the dubbed French voice instantly switches to a male voice.

11
00:01:09.563 --> 00:01:10.424
[Channel 1, a man speaking English] Thank you, Claire.

12
00:01:11.524 --> 00:01:12.235
[Channel 2, translated in a male voice] Merci, Claire.

13
00:01:13.235 --> 00:01:21.935
[Narrator] Amazing! You can even choose the language, the voice, and the accent! Or simply turn on automatic detection for two people on stage!

14
00:01:22.735 --> 00:01:30.435
[Narrator] Look at the numbers! The translated voice starts just one second after each phrase or sentence ends, thanks to on-device AI!

15
00:01:31.035 --> 00:01:39.835
[Narrator] With more than 50 languages and accents to choose from, zero internet needed in the hall, and unmatched reliability thanks to automatic failover!

16
00:01:40.535 --> 00:01:45.835
[Narrator] So no hefty conference internet line fees, and no unpopular data centers used for AI!

17
00:01:46.535 --> 00:01:52.735
[Narrator] Setting up your headset system was the hardest part. Now, you can make it even more incredibly useful!

18
00:01:53.535 --> 00:01:57.435
[Narrator] Go ahead! Visit conferencecaptioning.com for a free demo today!

